before:
```swift
enum SizeError: Error { case tooSmall }
func checkedSize(_ size: Int) throws -> Int {
    if size < 1 { throw SizeError.tooSmall }
    return size
}
```
The error enum conforms to Error so its cases can be thrown.

```swift
do {
    let size = try checkedSize(0)
    print(size)
} catch {
    print("Choose a positive size")
}
```
Use this after checkedSize. Throwing skips the remaining statements in do and enters catch.

```swift
func announce() {
    defer { print("Finished") }
    print("Working")
}
announce()
```
The output is Working, then Finished. defer does not run its body immediately.

after:
```swift
enum SizeError: Error { case tooSmall }
func checkedSize(_ size: Int) throws -> Int {
    defer { print("Finished") }
    if size < 1 { throw SizeError.tooSmall }
    return size
}
do {
    print(try checkedSize(0))
} catch {
    print("Choose a positive size")
}
```
This prints Finished, then Choose a positive size.
